body:
I want to update the [SearchParameter](https://community.algolia.com/algoliasearch-helper-js/docs/SearchParameters.html) `restrictSearchableAttributes` according to a user selection in a dropdown next to the search box. 

Updating `search.searchParameters` like `search.restrictSearchableAttributes = 'mynumbers'` does not work.

How can I set searchParameters **after** the initial setup:

```
var search = instantsearch({
    ...
    searchParameters: {
        restrictSearchableAttributes: 'text',
    }
})

$('#x').on('click', function() {
    // How to update "restrictSearchableAttributes" here (and start a new search)?
    // ?

    // This does NOT work:
    search.restrictSearchableAttributes = 'mynumbers';
    search.start();
})
```

comments.body:
You would have to build your own [custom widget](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/documentation/#custom-widgets):

``` js
var customWidget = {
  init: function(options) {
    $('x').onClick(function() {
      options.helper.setQueryParameter('restrictSearchableAttributes', ...);
    });
  }
};

search.addWidget(customWidget);
```

Let me know.

Ah I think what I missed in the custom widget, you need to call helper.search() at the end of the line:

``` js
 options.helper.setQueryParameter('restrictSearchableAttributes', ...);
 options.helper.search();
```

I just tried this and it worked well:

``` js
var algoliasearch = require("algoliasearch");
var helper = require("algoliasearch-helper")
var client = algoliasearch('appid', 'key');
var helper = helper(client, 'indexName');
helper.setQueryParameter('restrictSearchableAttributes', ['categories']);
helper.search()
helper.setQueryParameter('restrictSearchableAttributes'); // not sent
helper.search()
```

The "helper" you are using is this: https://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-helper-js
